From: conda-forge
Subject: Fix bundled headers with old system kernel headers

strace 7.0 updated its bundled taskstats.h to require linux/time_types.h,
but did not bundle that header.  Use strace's existing fallback definitions.
See https://github.com/strace/strace/issues/405.

--- a/bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/taskstats.h
+++ b/bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/taskstats.h
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
 #define _LINUX_TASKSTATS_H
 
 #include <linux/types.h>
-#include <linux/time_types.h>
+#include "kernel_time_types.h"
 
 /* Format for per-task data returned to userland when
  *	- a task exits
